      "assistant_text": "According to [[write-journal]], the **Guarded Write Journal** describes how the guarded tool executor manages file writes with automatic rollback capability:\n\n- **Core function**: Before overwriting any file, the journal records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n- **Rollback mechanism**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created ones.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This provides atomic transaction-like behavior for writes without needing a database, since the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent never actually uses this rollback functionality since it has no write capability at all.",
